{"name":"Machinery","hex":"#9999aa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"machinery","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The machines constituting a production apparatus, in a plant etc., collectively.","The working parts of a machine as a group."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/machinery"}],"entries":[{"title":"Machinery (Demuth)","blocks":[{"text":"Machinery is a 1920 drawing by American artist Charles Demuth. The drawing depicts a piece of industrial machinery in his hometown of Lancaster, Pennsylvania. The work is currently in the collection of the Metropolitan Museum of Art."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Machinery_MET_DP234201.jpg/330px-Machinery_MET_DP234201.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machinery_(Demuth)","wikidata":"Q20190815"},{"title":"Machine","blocks":[{"text":"A machine is a thermodynamic system that uses power to apply forces and control movement to perform an action. The term is commonly applied to artificial devices, such as those employing engines or motors, but also to natural biological macromolecules, such as molecular machines. Machines can be driven by animals and human power, by natural forces such as wind and water, and by chemical, thermal, or electrical power, and include a system of mechanisms that shape the actuator input to achieve a specific application of output forces and movement. They can also include computers and sensors that monitor performance and plan movement, often called mechanical systems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Woman_operator_operating_milling_machine_-_DPLA_-_34dc4b36bfa1d73f44c4d6983b12f77c_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Woman_operator_operating_milling_machine_-_DPLA_-_34dc4b36bfa1d73f44c4d6983b12f77c_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine","wikidata":"Q11019"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Flint_hand_axe.JPG/500px-Flint_hand_axe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Flint_hand_axe.JPG/500px-Flint_hand_axe.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A flint hand axe was found in Winchester.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlint_hand_axe.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/De_re_metallica_-_stamp_ore_crusher_%28125711574%29.jpg/500px-De_re_metallica_-_stamp_ore_crusher_%28125711574%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/De_re_metallica_-_stamp_ore_crusher_%28125711574%29.jpg/1280px-De_re_metallica_-_stamp_ore_crusher_%28125711574%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/De_re_metallica_-_stamp_ore_crusher_%28125711574%29.jpg/500px-De_re_metallica_-_stamp_ore_crusher_%28125711574%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This ore crushing machine is powered by a water wheel.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADe_re_metallica_-_stamp_ore_crusher_(125711574).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Bonsack_machine.png/500px-Bonsack_machine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Bonsack_machine.png/1280px-Bonsack_machine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Bonsack_machine.png/500px-Bonsack_machine.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","